(7735199, 1274912, 103142, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Venser:</b></div><hr/><i> Title bothers me. <br/>It''s not correct English. <br/> <br/>Did you mean "The role of fathers are underrated"? <br/>As written, you need another word after "father''s" because it''s possessive. The father''s what is underrated? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Actually, if you want to be pedantic, I believe it should be "The role of fathers is underrated." of the fathers is a prepositional phrase. So the verb should agree with the singular "role" :)<br/> <br/>But this was my highest score, because fathers and their roles are underrated as a society. <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2022-12-21 16:35:51.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Venser: Title bothers me. It''s not correct English.  Did you mean "The role of fathers are underrated"? As written, you need another word after "father''s" because it''s possessive. The father''s what is underrated?   Actually, if you want to be pedantic, I believe it should be "The role of fathers is underrated." of the fathers is a prepositional phrase. So the verb should agree with the singular "role" :) But this was my highest score, because fathers and their roles are underrated as a society. ', '2022-12-21 16:35:14.000000', '2022-12-21 16:35:51.000000', 0),
